      "writtenOn": "2025-12-01T19:17:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per my last comment in aosp/3863270: seems we can\u0027t really trust the host to assign the needed cache tags? So pKVM should rather assign the needed cache tags on its own, every time when associating a BDF with an IOMMU domain (when setting a context or PASID entry)? And if so, we don\u0027t need these assign/unassign hypercalls from the host?",
      "revId": "2e73b9b5a3277b1228dc98577a372a2cd1cfd14c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b3d8e03e_7d286a83",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 50
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
